==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}
[[File:Ceres symbol (fixed width).svg|thumb|Ceres's planetary symbol]]

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ḱer-|id=grow}}
{{lbor|en|la|Cerēs}}, goddess of the bounty, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ḱer-||to grow, to nourish}}. More at [[create]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪəɹiːz/}}
* {{hyphenation|en|Ce|res}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q32102}}{{lb|en|Roman god}} The Roman [[goddess]] of [[agriculture]]; equivalent to the [[Greek]] goddess [[Demeter]].
# {{senseid|en|Q596}}{{lb|en|astronomy}} A celestial body [[orbit]]ing between [[Mars]] and [[Jupiter]], the largest [[asteroid]] and innermost [[dwarf planet]]; officially called '''1 Ceres'''.
# {{place|en|city|co/Stanislaus County|s/California|c/US}}.

